# SYNOPSIS

```text
protocol todhchai.pty.Control version 2
call mode() -> Mode
call setMode(mode: Mode)
call windowSize() -> WindowSize
call takeEnds(yes: Bool)
event event(event: Event)
event resized(size: WindowSize)
event hangup()
```

# DESCRIPTION

The program's side.

Protocol `todhchai.pty.Control`, version 2, of library `PtyIPC`, its messages in the one wire format (wire(6)).

| Method | Kind | Since | Ordinal |
| `mode` | call | 1 | `0x65cb3588b290aca0` |
| `setMode` | call | 1 | `0x534df026b98fd96a` |
| `windowSize` | call | 1 | `0x4e85e1db1a4cc96e` |
| `takeEnds` | call | 1 | `0x5187e30fc19b171e` |
| `event` | event | 1 | `0x36d42bb0d0fc53c5` |
| `resized` | event | 1 | `0x1e22cc312ea29001` |
| `hangup` | event | 2 | `0x3ce1415031c6db5e` |

: `takeEnds`
  Whether the controller takes ^D as an `end` event (a shell, whose
  own input goes on), or the pty ends the program's stdin (the
  default).
: `hangup`
  The terminal has gone (its keys ended): Plan 9's hangup note.

